<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Mingyu Guo | AI for Commerce and Defence</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Mingyu Guo researches agentic commerce, the economics of generative AI, and AI for drone and cyber defence, using algorithmic game theory and optimisation.">
  <link rel="icon" href="static/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
  <link rel="icon" href="static/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="static/apple-touch-icon.png">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="static/site.css">
</head>

<body>
  <div class="site-shell">
    <header class="profile-header">
      <div class="profile-photo-wrap">
        <img class="profile-photo" src="static/mingyu.jpg" alt="Mingyu Guo" />
      </div>
      <div class="profile-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Senior Lecturer · Adelaide University</p>
        <h1>Mingyu Guo</h1>
        <p class="lead">AI for commerce and defence, grounded in game theory and optimisation.</p>
        <div class="contact-list" aria-label="Contact information">
          <span>mingyu.guo at adelaide dot edu dot au</span>
          <span>4.19 Ingkarni Wardli Building</span>
          <span>Adelaide University, Australia</span>
        </div>
        <nav class="profile-links" aria-label="Profile links">
          <a href="mailto:mingyu.guo@adelaide.edu.au">Email</a>
          <a href="https://dblp.org/pid/62/5599-1.html">DBLP</a>
          <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=bxEKdzkAAAAJ&hl=en">Google Scholar</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mingyu-guo-97236b1b/">LinkedIn</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Page sections">
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="#collaboration">Collaboration</a>
      <a href="#publications">Publications</a>
      <a href="#grants">Grants</a>
      <a href="#students">Students</a>
      <a href="#opportunities">Opportunities</a>
      <a href="#talks">Talks</a>
    </nav>

    <main class="layout">
      <div class="main-column">
        <section id="about" class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Profile</p>
            <h2>About Me</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>I am a <strong>Senior Lecturer</strong>, <strong>Program Director of the Master of Computer Science</strong>, and <strong>Graduate Research Coordinator</strong> in the School of Computer Science and Information Technology, <em>Adelaide University</em>.</p>
            <p>I use <strong>algorithmic game theory</strong> and <strong>optimisation</strong> to study how AI systems make decisions when participants have competing interests. My research spans two themes:</p>
            <p><strong>Agentic Commerce and the Economics of Generative AI.</strong> I study how AI agents buy, sell and negotiate on behalf of people and organisations. Current work includes advertising in language-model responses, the procurement and pricing of AI services, and auction design for AI tokens.</p>
            <p><strong>AI for Drone and Cyber Defence.</strong> I develop algorithms for coordinating drone teams and protecting enterprise networks against cyber attacks. This work addresses how to choose effective strategies at scale while accounting for an adversary's responses, with support from defence and industry partners.</p>
            <p>Before joining Adelaide, I was a Lecturer at the <em>University of Liverpool</em>. I hold a Ph.D. in Computer Science from <em>Duke University</em>, where my dissertation was runner-up for the <em>Victor Lesser Distinguished Dissertation Award</em>. I also hold an M.S. in Applied Mathematics from the <em>University of Florida</em> and a B.S. in Mathematics from <em>Zhejiang University</em>.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="profile-highlights">
            <h3>Highlights</h3>
            <ul class="highlight-list" role="list">
              {% for highlight in highlights %}
              <li>
                <strong class="highlight-title">{{ highlight.title }}</strong>
                <span class="highlight-detail">{% if highlight.detail_html %}{{ highlight.detail_html | safe }}{% else %}{{ highlight.detail }}{% endif %}</span>
              </li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="collaboration" class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Research Partnerships</p>
            <h2>Industry Collaboration</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>I collaborate with industry and government on decision problems that combine AI, optimisation, and strategic interaction. Current and recent partnerships span defence and autonomous systems with <strong>Saab Australia</strong> and the <strong>Defence Science and Technology Group</strong>, cybersecurity with the <strong>Cyber Security Cooperative Research Centre</strong>, health operations with <strong>SA Pathology</strong>, and PropTech with <strong>DDDI Group</strong>.</p>
            <p>I welcome conversations about collaborative research, industry PhDs, grant partnerships, and translating algorithms into decision-support tools and prototypes. <a href="mailto:mingyu.guo@adelaide.edu.au">Contact me to discuss a potential collaboration.</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="publications" class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Research Output</p>
            <h2>Selected Publications</h2>
            <a href="publications.html">View all publications</a>
          </div>
          {% include "_publication_list.html.j2" %}
        </section>

        <section class="section mobile-news">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Updates</p>
            <h2>News</h2>
          </div>
          <ol class="news-list">
            {% for item in news %}
            <li>
              <time>{{ item.date }}</time>
              <span>{{ item.text_html | safe }}</span>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="opportunities" class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Prospective Students</p>
            <h2>PhD/MPhil Opportunities</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>I welcome enquiries from prospective PhD/MPhil students in multi-agent AI, generative AI, optimisation, and related areas. I do not currently have a funded scholarship available for international applicants. Relevant options include:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><a href="https://adelaideuni.edu.au/research/research-degrees/research-scholarships/">Adelaide University research scholarships for PhD and MPhil students.</a></li>
              <li>Self-financed PhD/MPhil. Please note that this option requires you to pay tuition fees.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="au-students" class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Projects</p>
            <h2>Project Opportunities for AU Students</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>Current Adelaide University students are welcome to contact me about Honours and research projects. A project may target a research publication, an industry-facing prototype, or both. Recent student work has involved researchers at CMU, Oxford, and Harvard, as well as industry partners.</p>
            <p>Topics can be shaped around research questions, practical applications, startup ideas, or applied systems.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="students" class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Mentoring</p>
            <h2>Higher Degree by Research Students</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="student-groups">
            <div>
              <h3>Active</h3>
              <ol class="student-list">
                {% for student in students if not student.finish_year %}
                <li>
                  <strong>{{ student.name }}</strong>
                  <span>{{ student.program }}, <em>{{ student.role }}</em>, started {{ student.entry_year }}</span>
                  <span>with {{ student.other_supervisors | join(" and ") }}</span>
                  <span class="topic">{{ student.topic }}</span>
                  {% if student.note_html %}<span>{{ student.note_html | safe }}</span>{% endif %}
                </li>
                {% endfor %}
              </ol>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Completed</h3>
              <ol class="student-list">
                {% for student in students if student.finish_year %}
                <li>
                  <strong>{{ student.name }}</strong>
                  <span>{{ student.program }}, <em>{{ student.role }}</em>, {{ student.entry_year }}-{{ student.finish_year }}</span>
                  <span>with {{ student.other_supervisors | join(" and ") }}</span>
                  <span class="topic">{{ student.topic }}</span>
                  {% if student.note_html %}<span>{{ student.note_html | safe }}</span>{% endif %}
                </li>
                {% endfor %}
              </ol>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="grants" class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Funding</p>
            <h2>Research Grants</h2>
          </div>
          <ul class="grant-list">
            {% for grant in grants %}
            <li>
              <strong>{{ grant.title }}</strong>
              <span>{{ grant.role }} · {{ grant.funder }} · {{ grant.amount }} · {{ grant.duration }}</span>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Service</p>
            <h2>Selected Professional Service</h2>
          </div>
          <ul class="service-list">
            {% for service in services %}
            <li><strong>{{ service.role }}</strong>{% if service.detail %}<span>{{ service.detail }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="talks" class="section">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-kicker">Invited Talks</p>
            <h2>Selected Invited Talks</h2>
          </div>
          <ol class="talk-list">
            {% for presentation in presentations %}
            <li>
              <strong>{{ presentation.title }}</strong>
              <span>{% for event in presentation.events %}{{ event | safe }}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</span>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ol>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="side-column">
        <section class="side-panel desktop-news">
          <div class="section-heading compact">
            <p class="section-kicker">Updates</p>
            <h2>News</h2>
          </div>
          <ol class="news-list">
            {% for item in news %}
            <li>
              <time>{{ item.date }}</time>
              <span>{{ item.text_html | safe }}</span>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ol>
        </section>

      </aside>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <span>Last Updated: {{ last_updated }}</span>
      <span>Agentic commerce | Drone and cyber defence | Game theory and optimisation</span>
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>

</html>
